			<div class="content" id="post-content-4844076">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Emotional</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> ACS</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> This SCP is both the day of June the 31st and the global event that occurs on that day. During the day, members of the public appear to be in a state of complete wholeness and engage in unorthodox, but not unnatural activities. These activities can range from having a picnic in the park, gardening, napping in a graveyard to hugging and weeping. Knowledge of the day appears to be instinctive. People seem to remember it the moment the day begins and steadily forget about it when it finishes<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-75638-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-75638-1')">1</a></sup>. It also appears that those working for or associated with the Foundation are exempt from this event and are able to remember the happenings of the day. They also don't feel the state of wholeness that the general public experience on the day.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> <em>Something is in the air. Like an uncanny calm. Almost as if the whole world had sighed with relief and tranquility.</em></p>
<p>The overall story of this SCP is the strange, tranquil state the world enters on June the 31st, the day no-one will remember. Throughout the day, people enter a mindset they will rarely enter on any other day. Everyone is truly occupying their lives. That is, everyone except those in the Foundation, as they appear to be exempt from the SCP's effect. This is further emphasised when Foundation researchers interview people during the SCP. The interviewee treats foundation staff with slight pity and compassion, as if the Foundation is a child who doesn't understand something.</p>
<p>It's suggested that the SCP is necessary in some way. During one experiment, people were subjected to a strong narcotic and skipped the day entirely. Upon waking up, the subject appeared distant, mournful and depressive and continued in this state throughout their lives. It would appear that this SCP maintains a kind of wellbeing inside humanity.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> What I'm really trying to get across is both a feeling of calm peace experienced by the public and a sort of sad envy and exclusion experienced by the Foundation Staff. I haven't seen an SCP which does something beautiful and emphasises the loss Foundation Staff experience when they join the Foundation.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
<em>As a courtesy to our readers on mobile devices, please collapse long posts. ~Zyn</em>
