			<div class="content" id="post-content-4844960">
									

<blockquote>
<p>It's a great idea but there are a lot of questions here.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Good. Questions help deepen things. Answeres below:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>It just feels like it is being done to isolate The Foundation and that needs to be explained.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It is meant to isolate the Foundation. This whole SCP is meant to make the Foundation feel left out and make them question what they have lost by becoming a part of this scary, bizarre world. I'll explain it like this:</p>
<p>This SCP is to do with our habitation of our own lives. On June the 31st, all of humanity have one day in which they inhabit their lives completely. This means they achieve a kind of wholeness within their minds. They don't worry about what's coming or going, or think about how they are perceived or judged. They are simply in the moment. Think of it like this. How much of our lives do we actually inhabiting. We work, we sleep, we wonder, we worry and we think. And we try and give that meaning, which suggested some kind of dissatisfaction. But on this one day, humanity experience a state of existence free of meaning and instead are just being. A bit like Nirvana in Buddhism but instead of separating themselves from their lives, they emerce themselves in it. Taking ever part of their existence into their minds<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-742169-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-742169-1')">1</a></sup>.</p>
<p>Now to add the element of the Foundation to this SCP. The Foundation regularly deal with things that are outside the norm. Be it a toaster that has to be referred in the first person, a colossal sea serpant or an actual god. Because fo this, I'd imagine it's incredibly difficult for anyone who is a part of The Foundation to separate themselves from this Fantastic<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-742169-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-742169-2')">2</a></sup> world and focus on their short, slightly-blasé lives. They're like Rick from Rick and Morty. They've gained knowledge, power and perception but have had to abandon the simple comforts of everyday life. The Foundation can't partake in this SCP because they can't see and understand the world as they did before.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Why do people not notice the missing day?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If your talking like mathematically or scientifically, The Foundation deal with that. Twigging a few number and word here and their should be hard.</p>
<p>If your talking about the fact people forget the SCP, they forget because is will keep them sane. You experience a mode of being that is nigh-impossible to achieve in everyday. How would you feel if you suddenly returned to a strife filled, noisy, tedious life. Pretty bummed out and angry I'm guessing. And that's why they forget. Now you could ask, &quot;Then what's the point of this SCP at all?&quot;. My answer is, I don't know really. I think it's to keep the human race just sane and comfortable enough to keep going. To continue on with their lives without breaking down, going mad and screaming. This SCP is helping humanity, not hurting it.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Heck, why not other individuals?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It is perfectly possible that other individuals are like the Foundation and don't experience this SCP. But I'd argue this is very rare as in order for you not to experience this SCP, your perception of the world has had to change significantly. Other organisations like <strong>The Church of the Broken God</strong>, <strong>Parawatch</strong> or <strong>The Horizon Initiative</strong> may also be exempt from this SCP but I don't really care about them. In this SCP, the only parties in focus are The Foundation and the rest of mankind.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>What happens to the rest of the world? Do birds freeze, or what about rivers and currents?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>No, nothing freezes or stops. The rest of the world continues as if it was a normal day. I must note that on this day, it's not like all sunny and jolly, like a children's book. The environment doesn't change during this SCP. Only people's attitude, outlook, perception and memories.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>And keep in mind that there are people giving birth, suffering from imminent death, and any number of other medical conditions.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That changes nothing. It doesn't matter whether they're in pain or in pleasure. What matters is their perception and focus of it.</p>
